### Tested versions

- Godot 4.7.0
- .NET 9
- C# 14

### System information

Windows 10

### Issue description

`MustBeVariantAnalyzer` reports GD0303 when a C# 14 extension member (declared in
an `extension` block) is called with explicit type arguments.

The code is plain C# - no Godot types, and compiles fine in
a non-Godot project.

`GD0303: The parent symbol 'FooExtensions.extension<IntProvider, int>(IntProvider).GetNumber()' of a type argument that must be Variant compatible was not handled`

Docs say GD0303 is an engine bug and should be reported:
https://docs.godotengine.org/en/4.7/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/diagnostics/GD0303.html

### Steps to reproduce

Minimal code to reproduce:

```csharp
using System;
using System.Numerics;

public interface IHaveNumber<TNumber> where TNumber : INumber<TNumber> {
	static virtual TNumber GetNumber() => TNumber.Zero;
}

public static class FooExtensions {
	extension<T, TNumber>(T) where T : IHaveNumber<TNumber> where TNumber : INumber<TNumber> {
		public static TNumber GetNumber() => T.GetNumber();
	}
}

public class IntProvider : IHaveNumber<int> { }

public static class Program {
	public static void Main() {
		int num = IntProvider.GetNumber<IntProvider, int>();
		Console.WriteLine(num);
	}
}
```

