### Tested versions

Found in Godot 4.5.1.mono (custom build with [Voxel](https://github.com/Zylann/godot_voxel) as an engine module)

### System information

Godot v4.5.1.custom.mono (59a40ddbb) - Linux Mint 22.3 (Zena) on X11 - X11 display driver, Multi-window, 2 monitors - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3070 (nvidia; 590.48.01) - 13th Gen Intel(R) Core(TM) i7-13700K (24 threads) - 31.08 GiB memory

### Issue description

Based on the documentation, encountering diagnose GD0303 should be reported. 

The issue appears when using the new extension syntax introduced in c#14 in conjunction with type parameters.

The issue still happens if: 
- the type parameter and the struct is annotated with `[MustBeVariant]`
- the type parameter is given constraints like `T : struct` or `T : unmanaged`

The issue does NOT happen when: 

- switching to the old extension method syntax
- the type argument is inferred instead of explicit

### Steps to reproduce

Copy the following into an empty project:

```csharp
public static class MRP
{
    static void Test()
    {
        var container = new Container<Vector3>();
        var valueExplicit = container.GetValueNexSyntax<Vector3>(); // Error GD0303
        var valueInferred = container.GetValueNexSyntax(); // No error
        var valueOldSyntax = container.GetValueOldSyntax<Vector3>(); // No error
    }

    extension<T>(in Container<T> container)
    {
        public T GetValueNexSyntax() => container.Value;
    }

    public static T GetValueOldSyntax<T>(this in Container<T> container) => container.Value;

    public struct Container<T>
    {
        public T Value;
    }
}
```

